    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1682">

                <pb facs="1428" n="1324" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.114M69/150.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ottoman authorities, without replying to my repeated requests for surrender
                    of captain of <hi rendition="#italic">Texas</hi>, began proceedings against <pb
                        facs="1429" n="1325" xml:id="pg1325"/> him in the criminal court, Smyrna, on
                    the 9th instant. The Greek Consul, Smyrna, was notified, and the Greek Dragoman
                    attended the trial, which was postponed until July 30. I have again protested
                    and renewed request for surrender to our jurisdiction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rockhill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
